The problem: When processing the **second PDF** (fileIndex = 1), the code tries to call `mergedPdf.getPage(newPageIndex)` with an index that references pages that haven't been added to the merged document yet. The pages are copied but the annotations are being processed BEFORE all pages are actually added to the mergedPdf.

## Solution

Refactor the merge logic to use a **two-pass approach**:

1. **First pass**: Copy and add all pages from all PDFs to the merged document (without processing annotations)
2. **Second pass**: Process all annotations and update their page references

This ensures all pages exist in the merged document before we try to reference them.

